        {
            "id": "a6f07cea-dc35-4e8c-bc87-a29ce35c5c04",
            "build_id": "a2acf0dc-0805-4937-a1ec-e7fac3f0384d",
            "round_number": 5,
            "cash_earned": 0,
            "created_at": "2025-09-07T19:15:32.13296+00:00",
            "notes": "This round has the most flexibility in powers, usually it's Volley \u00e0 Deux as the shots will hit tanks often for the full damage, and it can be an easy bonus shot into a squishy in 1v1 duels.\n\nIf you're hurting for heals and your supports are playing with their monitors off, Forager can be very helpful as you'll naturally get healed for a tonne of health after every quick dash in the 1v1 duels.\n\nIf the enemy is going very hard into massive life pools or big shield builds Deep Pockets is a sleeper as it gives you all the ammo you'll need to be constantly burning them down. Redux is similar, though better against the armoured tanks rather than the shield ones who block it's effect if the Take-Aim bolt hits their shield.\n\nWe're just scaling the damage output now in this round, keeping the anti-tank item from the previous rounds and leaning heavily into whatever gives us the most weapon power. We should be able to get our big attack items this round.\n\nIf we're getting easy picks on supports, consider Portable Zipline as the dash resets just give us so much more Take-Aim opportunities that the relatively low 10% weapon power is greatly offset by simply firing so much more often. This works best against relatively static supports like scoped Ana players, Zenyattas and Lucio players who think they need to take a closeup 1v1 with you.\n\nAt this point green items are only to fill an awkward 6th slot or for Heartbeat Sensor which still cleans up in 1v1s, especially vs Reaper/Genji/Soldier.",
